			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement native file descriptor API and refine Tauri window handlers\n\nComplete the implementation of the `nativeHost` IPC surface by adding `file:open` and `file:close` handlers. These functions establish a process-global file descriptor table (backed by `HashMap<u32, File>` and `AtomicU32`) to support VS Code's `DiskFileSystemProvider` for large binary I/O, replacing previous full-read/write fallbacks.\n\nRefine window management handlers: implement `setDocumentEdited` for the macOS dirty-dot indicator, `setMinimumSize` to prevent workbench collapse, and `positionWindow` for multi-window restoration. Update `setRepresentedFilename` to display the filename component in the title bar. Re-evaluate `is_alive` connection logic to remove artificial sleep delays.\n\nOptimize `tree-view/create` event emission in `EnqueueTreeViewEmit` by migrating from per-call `tokio::spawn` to a persistent mpsc channel with a 16ms frame-aligned batcher. This eliminates task overhead during boot. Additionally, reduce the terminal startup delay from 120ms to 20ms, matching M-series hardware capabilities, and improve `LifecyclePhaseState` formatting.",
			"SHA": "8cde99c082f32ec6c8726e947e7a696d2c3ccf7e"
		},
